IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- PART 10A, TRANSFER OF REGISTRATION: s 362 (revocation of registration), lines 23405 to 23475 of CoA1967.txt.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is the text's yes; JUST FALSE is the text's no in its own words; NOTHING is "the text does not say"
-- (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sge)"). A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- Whether the company "fails to comply with section 359(6)" is s 359(6)'s question (sge-p10a-359.l4); here it is a plain input.

DECLARE `s 362 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 362(2)(a) and (b) give the company written notice of the Registrar's intention to revoke the registration, specifying a period of at least 30 days for written representations`
    `s 362(2)(c) consider the company's written representations`
    `s 362(2)(b) make written representations to the Registrar`
    `s 362(4)(a) cause a notice of the order of revocation to be published in the Gazette`
    `s 362(4)(b) serve a copy of the notice of the order of revocation on the company`

§ `Section 362(1): the Registrar may revoke`

-- "The Registrar may by order revoke the registration of a company if the company fails to comply with section 359(6)."
-- src:23407 | 362.—(1) The Registrar may by order revoke the registration of a
-- src:23408 | company if the company fails to comply with section 359(6).
@ref s 362(1) (src:23407-23408)
GIVEN `the company has failed to comply with section 359(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(1) the Registrar may by order revoke the registration of the company` MEANS
    IF `the company has failed to comply with section 359(6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("The Registrar may by order revoke ... if the company fails to comply with section 359(6)") whose "if" gate failed (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line F-362-1 in NOTES.md)

§ `Section 362(2): what the Registrar must do before making an order`

-- "(a) give the company written notice of the Registrar's intention to revoke the registration" and "(b) specify in the notice a period of at
-- least 30 days within which the company may make written representations to the Registrar".
-- src:23415 | (2) The Registrar must, before making an order of revocation —
-- src:23417 | (a) give the company written notice of the Registrar’s
-- src:23418 | intention to revoke the registration;
@ref s 362(2)(a) (src:23415-23418)
GIVEN `the Registrar has given the company written notice of the Registrar's intention to revoke the registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(2)(a) the Registrar has given the company written notice of the intention to revoke the registration` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has given the company written notice of the Registrar's intention to revoke the registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must, before making an order of revocation — (a) give the company written notice of the Registrar's intention to revoke the registration"

-- src:23415 | (2) The Registrar must, before making an order of revocation —
-- src:23420 | (b) specify in the notice a period of at least 30 days within
-- src:23421 | which the company may make written representations to
-- src:23422 | the Registrar; and
@ref s 362(2)(b) (src:23415-23422)
GIVEN `the number of days the notice specifies for the company to make written representations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(2)(b) the notice specifies a period of at least 30 days for written representations` MEANS
    IF `the number of days the notice specifies for the company to make written representations` AT LEAST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) specify in the notice a period of at least 30 days within which the company may make written representations to the Registrar"

-- (c) "consider the company's written representations (if any) that are received by the Registrar within the time specified in the notice".
-- src:23415 | (2) The Registrar must, before making an order of revocation —
-- src:23424 | (c) consider the company’s written representations (if any)
-- src:23425 | that are received by the Registrar within the time specified
-- src:23426 | in the notice.
@ref s 362(2)(c) (src:23415-23426)
GIVEN `the company made written representations that the Registrar received within the time specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has considered the company's written representations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(2)(c) the Registrar has considered the company's written representations` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company made written representations that the Registrar received within the time specified in the notice`)
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the paragraph asks the Registrar to consider representations "(if any)": with none received in time there is nothing to consider (fork line F-362-2 in NOTES.md)
    ELSE (IF `the Registrar has considered the company's written representations`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) consider the company's written representations (if any) that are received by the Registrar within the time specified in the notice"

-- src:23415 | (2) The Registrar must, before making an order of revocation —
-- src:23417 | (a) give the company written notice of the Registrar’s
-- src:23418 | intention to revoke the registration;
-- src:23420 | (b) specify in the notice a period of at least 30 days within
-- src:23421 | which the company may make written representations to
-- src:23422 | the Registrar; and
-- src:23424 | (c) consider the company’s written representations (if any)
-- src:23425 | that are received by the Registrar within the time specified
-- src:23426 | in the notice.
@ref s 362(2) (src:23415-23426)
GIVEN `the Registrar has given the company written notice of the Registrar's intention to revoke the registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days the notice specifies for the company to make written representations` IS A NUMBER
      `the company made written representations that the Registrar received within the time specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has considered the company's written representations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(2) the Registrar has done what the subsection requires before making an order of revocation` MEANS
    IF    `s 362(2)(a) the Registrar has given the company written notice of the intention to revoke the registration` `the Registrar has given the company written notice of the Registrar's intention to revoke the registration` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `s 362(2)(b) the notice specifies a period of at least 30 days for written representations` `the number of days the notice specifies for the company to make written representations` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `s 362(2)(c) the Registrar has considered the company's written representations` `the company made written representations that the Registrar received within the time specified in the notice` `the Registrar has considered the company's written representations` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must, before making an order of revocation — (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ..."

-- The Registrar's duties as a regulative rule: notice (with the period), then consideration of what comes in. The text states no time limit
-- and no consequence, so no trace can show it breached.
-- src:23415 | (2) The Registrar must, before making an order of revocation —
-- src:23417 | (a) give the company written notice of the Registrar’s
-- src:23418 | intention to revoke the registration;
-- src:23420 | (b) specify in the notice a period of at least 30 days within
-- src:23421 | which the company may make written representations to
-- src:23422 | the Registrar; and
-- src:23424 | (c) consider the company’s written representations (if any)
-- src:23425 | that are received by the Registrar within the time specified
-- src:23426 | in the notice.
@ref s 362(2) (src:23415-23426)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 362 act`
`s 362(2) before making an order of revocation the Registrar must give notice and consider representations` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 362(2)(a) and (b) give the company written notice of the Registrar's intention to revoke the registration, specifying a period of at least 30 days for written representations`
    HENCE (PARTY Registrar
           MUST `s 362(2)(c) consider the company's written representations`
           HENCE FULFILLED)
           -- no LEST: s 362(2) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not consider the company's written representations before making an order of revocation" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]
    -- no LEST: s 362(2) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not give the company written notice of the intention to revoke the registration, with a period of at least 30 days, before making an order of revocation" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- What the company may do in that period (the right the notice gives it): "a period of at least 30 days within which the company may make
-- written representations". AT 0 is the day of the notice; `the number of days the notice specifies` is the period the notice names.
-- src:23415 | (2) The Registrar must, before making an order of revocation —
-- src:23420 | (b) specify in the notice a period of at least 30 days within
-- src:23421 | which the company may make written representations to
-- src:23422 | the Registrar; and
@ref s 362(2)(b) (src:23415-23422)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days the notice specifies for the company to make written representations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 362 act`
`s 362(2)(b) the company may make written representations within the period the notice specifies` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MAY `s 362(2)(b) make written representations to the Registrar`
    WITHIN `the number of days the notice specifies for the company to make written representations`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Section 362(3): the order`

-- "At the expiration of the time mentioned in the notice mentioned in subsection (2), the Registrar may, unless cause to the contrary is
-- previously shown, order that the registration of the company be revoked."
-- The time runs from the day the notice is given (the text does not say, fork line F-362-3). The order may be made on a day after the last day
-- of the period, not on or before it ("At the expiration"). A notice that specifies fewer than 30 days is not "the notice mentioned in
-- subsection (2)". An "upon"-type gate and an "unless" gate on a "may": JUST FALSE for each (NOTES.md, Split sites (sge); F-362-4).
-- src:23430 | (3) At the expiration of the time mentioned in the notice mentioned
-- src:23431 | in subsection (2), the Registrar may, unless cause to the contrary is
-- src:23432 | previously shown, order that the registration of the company be
-- src:23433 | revoked.
@ref s 362(3) (src:23430-23433)
GIVEN `the date the notice of the intention to revoke the registration was given` IS A DATE
      `the number of days the notice specifies for the company to make written representations` IS A NUMBER
      `the date on which the Registrar would make the order` IS A DATE
      `cause to the contrary has been shown to the Registrar before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(3) the Registrar may order that the registration of the company be revoked` MEANS
    IF `the number of days the notice specifies for the company to make written representations` LESS THAN 30
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notice mentioned in subsection (2)" is a notice specifying a period of at least 30 days; a shorter one is not that notice, so the power does not arise
    ELSE (IF `the date on which the Registrar would make the order` AT MOST `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the notice of the intention to revoke the registration was given` `the number of days the notice specifies for the company to make written representations` Days
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "At the expiration of the time mentioned in the notice" (the time has not expired; an "upon"-type gate on a "may": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (b) and (c))
          ELSE (IF `cause to the contrary has been shown to the Registrar before that date`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Registrar may, unless cause to the contrary is previously shown, order" (the "unless" is met)
                ELSE JUST TRUE))

§ `Section 362(4): after the order`

-- "(a) cause a notice of the order of revocation to be published in the Gazette" and "(b) serve a copy of the notice of the order of
-- revocation on the company which registration is revoked".
-- src:23437 | (4) The Registrar must —
-- src:23439 | (a) cause a notice of the order of revocation to be published in
-- src:23440 | the Gazette; and
@ref s 362(4)(a) (src:23437-23440)
GIVEN `the Registrar has caused a notice of the order of revocation to be published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(4)(a) the Registrar has caused a notice of the order of revocation to be published in the Gazette` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has caused a notice of the order of revocation to be published in the Gazette`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must — (a) cause a notice of the order of revocation to be published in the Gazette"

-- src:23437 | (4) The Registrar must —
-- src:23442 | (b) serve a copy of the notice of the order of revocation on the
-- src:23443 | company which registration is revoked.
@ref s 362(4)(b) (src:23437-23443)
GIVEN `the Registrar has served a copy of the notice of the order of revocation on the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(4)(b) the Registrar has served a copy of the notice of the order of revocation on the company` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has served a copy of the notice of the order of revocation on the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must — (b) serve a copy of the notice of the order of revocation on the company which registration is revoked"

-- src:23437 | (4) The Registrar must —
-- src:23439 | (a) cause a notice of the order of revocation to be published in
-- src:23440 | the Gazette; and
-- src:23442 | (b) serve a copy of the notice of the order of revocation on the
-- src:23443 | company which registration is revoked.
@ref s 362(4) (src:23437-23443)
GIVEN `the Registrar has caused a notice of the order of revocation to be published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has served a copy of the notice of the order of revocation on the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(4) the Registrar has published and served the notice of the order of revocation` MEANS
    IF    `s 362(4)(a) the Registrar has caused a notice of the order of revocation to be published in the Gazette` `the Registrar has caused a notice of the order of revocation to be published in the Gazette` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `s 362(4)(b) the Registrar has served a copy of the notice of the order of revocation on the company` `the Registrar has served a copy of the notice of the order of revocation on the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must — (a) ...; and (b) ..."

-- The duties as a regulative rule: publish, then serve. No time limit and no consequence is stated: no breach path.
-- src:23437 | (4) The Registrar must —
-- src:23439 | (a) cause a notice of the order of revocation to be published in
-- src:23440 | the Gazette; and
-- src:23442 | (b) serve a copy of the notice of the order of revocation on the
-- src:23443 | company which registration is revoked.
@ref s 362(4) (src:23437-23443)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 362 act`
`s 362(4) the Registrar must publish the notice of the order of revocation and serve a copy on the company` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 362(4)(a) cause a notice of the order of revocation to be published in the Gazette`
    HENCE (PARTY Registrar
           MUST `s 362(4)(b) serve a copy of the notice of the order of revocation on the company`
           HENCE FULFILLED)
           -- no LEST: s 362(4) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not serve a copy of the notice of the order of revocation on the company" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    -- no LEST: s 362(4) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not cause a notice of the order of revocation to be published in the Gazette" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

§ `Section 362(5): the order takes effect on publication`

-- "Upon publication of the notice of the order of revocation in the Gazette, the order of revocation takes effect and the company ceases to be
-- a company as defined in section 4(1) and the provisions of this Act cease to apply to the company."
-- Three effects, all "Upon publication": from the day of publication (and not before it, and not at all if it has not been published) each
-- is JUST TRUE; before that, JUST FALSE ("upon" read as "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (b) and (c); fork line F-362-5).
-- src:23447 | (5) Upon publication of the notice of the order of revocation in the
-- src:23448 | Gazette, the order of revocation takes effect and the company ceases
@ref s 362(5) (src:23447-23448)
GIVEN `the notice of the order of revocation has been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice of the order of revocation was published in the Gazette` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 362(5) the day is on or after the publication of the notice of the order of revocation in the Gazette` MEANS
    `the notice of the order of revocation has been published in the Gazette` AND `the date asked about` AT LEAST `the date the notice of the order of revocation was published in the Gazette`

-- src:23447 | (5) Upon publication of the notice of the order of revocation in the
-- src:23448 | Gazette, the order of revocation takes effect and the company ceases
@ref s 362(5) (src:23447-23448)
GIVEN `the notice of the order of revocation has been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice of the order of revocation was published in the Gazette` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(5) the order of revocation has taken effect` MEANS
    IF `s 362(5) the day is on or after the publication of the notice of the order of revocation in the Gazette` `the notice of the order of revocation has been published in the Gazette` `the date the notice of the order of revocation was published in the Gazette` `the date asked about`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon publication of the notice of the order of revocation in the Gazette, the order of revocation takes effect" (before publication it has not)

-- src:23447 | (5) Upon publication of the notice of the order of revocation in the
-- src:23448 | Gazette, the order of revocation takes effect and the company ceases
-- src:23449 | to be a company as defined in section 4(1) and the provisions of this
-- src:23450 | Act cease to apply to the company.
@ref s 362(5) (src:23447-23450)
GIVEN `the notice of the order of revocation has been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice of the order of revocation was published in the Gazette` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(5) the company has ceased to be a company as defined in section 4(1)` MEANS
    IF `s 362(5) the day is on or after the publication of the notice of the order of revocation in the Gazette` `the notice of the order of revocation has been published in the Gazette` `the date the notice of the order of revocation was published in the Gazette` `the date asked about`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon publication of the notice of the order of revocation in the Gazette, ... the company ceases to be a company as defined in section 4(1)" (before publication it has not)

-- src:23447 | (5) Upon publication of the notice of the order of revocation in the
-- src:23448 | Gazette, the order of revocation takes effect and the company ceases
-- src:23449 | to be a company as defined in section 4(1) and the provisions of this
-- src:23450 | Act cease to apply to the company.
@ref s 362(5) (src:23447-23450)
GIVEN `the notice of the order of revocation has been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice of the order of revocation was published in the Gazette` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(5) the provisions of this Act have ceased to apply to the company` MEANS
    IF `s 362(5) the day is on or after the publication of the notice of the order of revocation in the Gazette` `the notice of the order of revocation has been published in the Gazette` `the date the notice of the order of revocation was published in the Gazette` `the date asked about`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon publication of the notice of the order of revocation in the Gazette, ... the provisions of this Act cease to apply to the company" (before publication they have not)

§ `Section 362(6): the order is final`

-- "An order of revocation under subsection (3) is final."
-- src:23454 | (6) An order of revocation under subsection (3) is final.
@ref s 362(6) (src:23454-23454)
GIVEN `the order is an order of revocation made under section 362(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(6) the order of revocation is final` MEANS
    IF `the order is an order of revocation made under section 362(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of "An order of revocation under subsection (3)" only

§ `Section 362(7): liability continues`

-- "Despite the order of revocation in respect of a company under subsection (3), the liability (if any) of every officer and member of the
-- company continues." "(if any)": the subsection continues a liability that exists and creates none.
-- src:23458 | (7) Despite the order of revocation in respect of a company under
-- src:23459 | subsection (3), the liability (if any) of every officer and member of the
-- src:23460 | company continues.
@ref s 362(7) (src:23458-23460)
GIVEN `an order of revocation has been made under section 362(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a liability in respect of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(7) the liability of the person continues despite the order of revocation` MEANS
    IF (NOT `an order of revocation has been made under section 362(3)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Despite the order of revocation in respect of a company under subsection (3)": the subsection speaks of liability after such an order and says nothing before one
    ELSE (IF (NOT `the person is an officer of the company`) AND (NOT `the person is a member of the company`)
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "the liability (if any) of every officer and member of the company continues" names officers and members and says nothing of anyone else
          ELSE (IF `the person has a liability in respect of the company`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the liability (if any)": the subsection continues a liability that exists and says nothing where there is none

§ `Section 362(8): rights and claims are not prejudiced`

-- "Nothing in this section prejudices — (a) the enforcement by any person of any right or claim against the company; or (b) the enforcement by
-- the company of any right or claim against any person."
DECLARE `s 362(8) enforcement` IS ONE OF
    `s 362(8)(a) the enforcement by a person of a right or claim against the company`
    `s 362(8)(b) the enforcement by the company of a right or claim against a person`
    `s 362(8) some other enforcement`

-- src:23464 | (8) Nothing in this section prejudices —
-- src:23466 | (a) the enforcement by any person of any right or claim against
-- src:23467 | the company; or
-- src:23469 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026
-- src:23470 | 475 Companies Act 1967 2020 Ed.
-- src:23472 | (b) the enforcement by the company of any right or claim
-- src:23473 | against any person.
@ref s 362(8) (src:23464-23473)
GIVEN `the enforcement of the right or claim` IS A `s 362(8) enforcement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(8) section 362 prejudices the enforcement of the right or claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the enforcement of the right or claim`
    WHEN `s 362(8)(a) the enforcement by a person of a right or claim against the company` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section prejudices — (a) the enforcement by any person of any right or claim against the company"
    WHEN `s 362(8)(b) the enforcement by the company of a right or claim against a person` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section prejudices — (b) the enforcement by the company of any right or claim against any person"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Nothing in this section prejudices" two kinds of enforcement and says nothing of any other
